     iiggcc — Intel Ethernet Controller I225 driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee iifflliibb
           ddeevviiccee iiggcc

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_igc_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiggcc driver provides support for any PCI Express adapter or LOM (LAN
     On Motherboard) based on the Intel I225 Multi Gigabit Controller.  The
     driver supports Transmit/Receive checksum offload, Jumbo Frames, MSI/MSI-
     X, TSO, and RSS.

     Support for Jumbo Frames is provided via the interface MTU setting.  Se‐
     lecting an MTU larger than 1500 bytes with the ifconfig(8) utility con‐
     figures the adapter to receive and transmit Jumbo Frames.  The maximum
     MTU size for Jumbo Frames is 9216 bytes.

     This driver version supports VLAN hardware insertion / extraction, and
     VLAN checksum offload.  For information on enabling VLANs, see
     ifconfig(8).  The iiggcc driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enables auto-negotiation for speed and duplex.

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Sets 10Mbps operation.  Use the mmeeddiiaaoopptt option to select
                  hhaallff--dduupplleexx mode.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX    Sets 100Mbps operation.  Use the mmeeddiiaaoopptt option to select
                  hhaallff--dduupplleexx mode.

     11000000bbaasseeTT    Sets 1000Mbps operation.  Only ffuullll--dduupplleexx mode is supported
                  at this speed.

     22550000bbaasseeTT    Sets 2500Mbps operation.  Only ffuullll--dduupplleexx mode is supported
                  at this speed.

